      },
      "cr": 1,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Toadburt.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. XP ledger: level 2, power rating 5 → CR 1 as a operative. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>From Leashed Agent to Indentured Archivist</strong> — Formerly Iron Legion (coerced), currently Shadow Estate Archives (indentured)</p><p>Status: Active — real injured Toadburt confirmed alive at the Shadow Estate portal circle with Tanukiburt and Mystic Morel</p><p>Toadburt's story is a masterclass in trading one cage for another. The Iron Legion strapped an entropy ring on him and sent him into the Feywild as a coerced operative. Now the ring is off, but Toadburt isn't free—he's working for the Shadow Estate's Archivist in exchange for gradual healing, recovering from his injuries over two-week intervals while organizing books in a vampire library. Waluigi recognizes this pattern: someone too damaged to refuse help, accepting terms from whoever offers it, trading independence for survival. It's not slavery. It's not freedom. It's the grey area in between that nobody likes to name. The Toadburt question has changed from unresolved suspicion to immediate rescue problem. Remi's exterior scouting confirmed an injured real Toadburt gathered at the master-bedroom portal circle with Tanukiburt and Mystic Morel while the rug was being covered and uncovered. This means Toadburt is alive, not free, and positioned at the exact route the party needs to use.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Dagger</strong> — “From Leashed Agent to Indentured Archivist”</li><li><strong>Keen Records</strong> — “From Leashed Agent to Indentured Archivist”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/toadburt</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/toadburt</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
